From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:48:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 118/144] GreatDANE: source-level check that updater.ini and
 About branding cover every locale (round 4d)

greatdane/tests/locale_branding_check.py (no build, no signing, no network) asserts:

- The generate_ini.py maintenance-description override is global, not a locale
  allowlist, and therefore covers every code in all-locales and shipped-locales
  (114 + 104, union 115 including en-US).
- Fixtures for de, fr, ja, zh-CN, en-GB and ar (unmodified mozilla-l10n copies,
  fetched 2026-11-10) plus en-US and synthetic leftover/missing-key inputs all
  produce the branded Dane MozillaMaintenanceDescription, with no leftover
  "Mozilla Firefox" / "Firefox". Official Firefox / Mozilla Firefox display
  names keep the localized wording.
- The proposed About attribution, disassociation sentence, and trademark notice
  are in greatdane brand.ftl, shipped to every locale via locales/jar.mn, kept
  in sync in en-US aboutDialog.ftl, and wired from aboutDialog.xhtml when
  MOZ_OFFICIAL_BRANDING is not set.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
